WEBVTT

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.840
That bike...

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.360
Hii-kun!

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.910
Hiroshi? What are you doing here?

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.490
I thought you went back to Tokyo.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.300
Udon...

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.770
I need to eat sanuki udon...

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.010
Comfort udon to heal my broken heart...

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.500
What?

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.680
<b>Poco's Udon World</b>

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.600
Episode 9: "Sardine Stock"

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.500
Tatami mats!

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.600
Tatami!

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.230
This house is huge!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.480
The town's, like, so puny!

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.350
Kagawa is totally in the sticks!

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:15.500
<i>Why is it, I wonder?</i>

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.190
<i>It's fine when I say that,</i>

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:21.020
<i>but hearing an outsider call it "the sticks"</i>

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.320
<i>ticks me off.</i>

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.250
Go eat your udon and go back 
to your oh-so-great Tokyo!

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.060
This is the house where 
Rinko-san grew up, isn't it?

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.370
Huh?

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.850
Rinko-san...

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:43.380
I know you were shocked 
about my sister, but...

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.640
<i>He's emotionally unstable.</i>

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.530
Overflowing with energy... I am Gaogao-chan.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.840
Your punches won't work on me.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.610
Little guy...

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.470
Th-This is...

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.520
This toy is discontinued and 
sells for a fortune in auctions!

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.410
It's a super rare find! How'd you get it?!

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.580
Oh, Manabu-san gave him that.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.090
Manabu-san?

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.650
W-Wait a second...

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:17.420
The person Dahama-san introduced 
you to was Saeki Manabu-san?

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.450
Yeah, what about it?

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.450
You met <i>the</i> legendary creative director?!

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.810
I was there, too... How could I have missed him?

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:27.990
No way...

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.880
Huh? What's the big deal?

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.350
Souta-san! Did you meet him 
without knowing a thing about him?!

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:32.650
Uh, yeah...

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.680
Saeki Manabu-san is best known 
as the creator of Gaogao-chan.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.500
He set off the Gaogao-chan boom!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.700
What? Him?

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:46.200
I love this island.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.080
I've set my roots down in the area, 
and I do craftsmanship with the locals.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.040
To me, this style is at the cutting edge.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.960
I think it's an ideal place.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.500
For my project to promote that,

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.810
someone with strengths in the Web and 
digital fields will be indispensable.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.210
And that's why...

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.820
I'd like to borrow your help.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.870
<i>I had no idea someone so amazing 
was working in Kagawa.</i>

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:13.780
Huh?

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.240
Poco?

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.260
Hiroshi?

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.480
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.480
<b>Udon</b>

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.480
Amazing!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.610
Wow, it's a perfect fit!

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.870
I like it here.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.000
What are you doing in here?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Souta-san, look!

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.540
The little guy fits in the pot.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.750
Wow!

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.000
<i>Right. I remember now.</i>

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.350
<i>He really startled me at first.</i>

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.360
<i>I never dreamed we'd end up living together.</i>

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:47.760
Souta-san!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.010
I have to...

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:52.310
I have to eat some comfort udon!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.980
There's an udon place nearby. 
You can eat there—

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:55.960
Souta-san!

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:56.810
What?

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:59.170
Let's make some udon!

00:04:59.170 --> 00:04:59.730
What?!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.940
Your place is an udon place, right?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.940
Yeah, but this is too out of the blue...

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.330
Right? Right?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.660
We make udon?

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.020
You too, Poco?

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.700
We make udon?

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.590
My dad didn't teach me how.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:16.350
I don't really know how to make udon.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.970
If you still want it anyway...

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:21.510
All right!

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.150
All right!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:25.090
All right! All right!

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.570
<b>Notes Part 1</b>

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.310
This is so cool! A secret recipe 
passed down from father to son!

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.970
It's not that big a deal.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.140
What are you wearing?

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.850
You just put water in here 
and knead it, right?

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.020
Wait, wait.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.930
It has to be salt water.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.260
I'll take care of this. You look 
for a thick plastic sheet.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:46.820
Got it.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.590
Hey now, Poco. Don't play with the flour.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.890
Th-They've come... The wash basin aliens!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.290
Over here, Poco.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.660
Poco, your ears! Your ears!

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.600
<i>I managed to muscle my way 
out of this last time...</i>

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.280
<i>But I'm not confident 
that I can trick him again.</i>

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:26.940
I'm counting on you, Poco.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.660
Pwomise.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.530
This should do it.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.570
So this is the dough?

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:35.700
It's not done yet.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.660
Souta.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.220
We do "one, two, one, two"?

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:44.040
That's right. How did you know?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.670
Huh? What are we doing?

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.390
You step on the dough.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.280
What?!

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.000
Are you sure that's okay?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.350
I'm a little reluctant to step on food...

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.190
You put it under plastic first, so it's fine.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:59.150
Besides, if you don't do it, 
it won't get elastic enough.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.970
Hey, why are you grinning?

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.110
Everybody does it, both pros and amateurs.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.320
Well, Souta-san...

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.850
You say you didn't learn how,

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.960
but it sure sounds like making 
udon is second nature to you.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.890
I-I don't know that much about udon.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:18.700
It's not...

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.140
Souta loves udon.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.470
You too, Poco?

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:31.010
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.440
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.440
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.940
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.940
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:38.000
Brings back memories.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.000
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.640
Huh? What does?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.600
Oh, my dad used to

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.830
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.200
step on udon like that.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:45.440
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.260
Oh, really?

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.280
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.920
Man, this takes a lot of stamina...

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.010
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.920
Souta-san, switch with me.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:53.780
One, two, udon, udon.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.460
So weak...

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:56.910
One, two, udon, udon...

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.890
One, two, udon, udon...

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.790
That's a funny shout.

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:03.750
One... two... udon... udon...

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.250
One...

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:13.070
What are you doing?

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:16.510
Oh, er... P-Poco's tummy was showing.

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:20.220
Jeez, Poco, your tum-tum will get cold.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.680
Your tail, your tail!

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:25.610
Just because his tummy might get cold? 
I think you're overreacting...

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.770
O-Oh, yeah! Poco, spring onions!

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.940
Can you get me some from the field?

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.210
You know what they are, right? Please.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:34.410
Spring onions!

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:40.660
Spring onions, spring onions, spring onions...

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:44.670
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:53.350
Pwomise, pwomise...

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:55.130
Go bye-bye, go bye-bye!

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.350
Go bye-bye, go bye-bye!

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:04.320
Pwomise, pwomise...

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:05.700
Go bye-bye..

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:17.200
Go bye-bye...

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:21.580
<b>Dried Konbu</b>

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.100
<b>Dried Sardines</b>

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:24.160
The dough will be ready after 
we let it sit a little longer.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.550
The soup stock is almost ready, too.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.920
That smells great.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.610
Hey, the little guy's taking a while.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.920
Want me to go check on him?

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.760
Uh, no! I'll go.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.610
He might have gone around back.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.930
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.820
Poco?

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.150
Poco!

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:47.190
Poco?

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.450
S-Souta...

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:57.830
Poco?!

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.570
What happened? Why...

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:00.970
You're almost all tanuki!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.450
You have to turn back quick.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:06.580
Are you saying...

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:09.290
You can't turn back into a human?

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:13.590
Souta-san! Little guy!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.350
Souta...

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.950
Poco, listen closely.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:27.100
Oh, Souta-san.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:28.780
Did you find him?

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.740
Souta-san?

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:34.890
What's up...

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.680
What the heck is that?

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:43.030
It's a tanuki.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.090
Kagawa's in the sticks,

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:48.040
so tanuki steal from the fields all the time.

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:55.800
I-It's definitely cute...

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.610
Its fluffy cheeks and tiny paws...

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:01.020
The way it's kinda chubby...

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:03.680
It somehow reminds me of the little guy.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:06.180
Y-You think so?

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.430
I don't know what you...

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.920
Souta-san?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.190
Wh-What?

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:16.440
You've been acting kind of suspicious.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:18.750
This isn't like you.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:22.250
The little guy's missing, and you're 
stopping to play with a tanuki?

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.760
Oh, er...

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:27.720
That Poco... He probably went to 
the old lady's house next door.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:31.000
Man, she has a really sharp tongue, you know...

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.670
Then shouldn't we go look for him?

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:36.010
Oh, uh, well...

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:36.800
Or...

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.020
Is there some reason not to
that has to do with the kid?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.310
It ran!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.560
The tanuki doesn't matter right now.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:54.760
We can't know that.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.940
I'm telling you, I saw it!

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.030
When you and the kid came to Tokyo,

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:03.080
the kid had ears and a tail!

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.690
It's been bugging me this whole time.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.760
I know I wasn't just seeing things.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.830
Listen, Hiroshi.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.050
If Poco really did

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:17.840
have ears and a tail, like you say...

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:20.090
So what?

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.290
D-Do you hear yourself, Souta-san?

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:24.840
It's obviously not normal!

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.890
You're Poco's friend, aren't you?

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:34.200
Would ears and a tail undo that?

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:38.600
What's wrong with being a little different?

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.240
That kid isn't normal.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:48.720
Oh, you mean our new programmer?

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:52.310
Right. He dresses weird, 
and he acts strange, too.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:55.090
I have no idea why Dahama-san 
hired a guy like him.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:56.900
Right, Tawara?

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:00.800
Hmm? Well, yeah. I guess he's different.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.130
But I don't think that's a bad thing.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:09.070
He's a fast worker, and if you talk 
to him, he's actually a nice guy.

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:10.100
Huh?

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.380
Really?

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:13.490
Hey.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.360
Dahama-san! How long have you been there?!

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.160
I have good hearing.

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.940
The guy who talked smack 
about me and Hiroshi...

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.240
That's a thousand-yen fine.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.870
F-For real?

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:28.950
Hiroshi...

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.760
Poco, listen closely.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.220
Can you turn completely 
into a tanuki right now?

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:49.270
While I distract Hiroshi, you run away.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.920
Stay hidden until this blows over.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:54.790
I promise I'll come get you later.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.230
Don't worry!

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:01.230
To me, you're Poco, 
no matter what you look like.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:07.780
<i>Souta.</i>

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.500
<i>Souta. Souta.</i>

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.290
<i>Souta!</i>

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.950
Souta-san... I...

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.560
I...

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:30.850
Why are you crying?!

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:33.190
No, I'm just...

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:39.230
Spring onions! Souta, spring onions!

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:40.630
Poco!

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:42.910
Great! Thanks!

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:46.730
See, Hiroshi? He doesn't have ears or a tail.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:46.730
No...

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.190
I don't care about that anymore.

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:53.370
I don't care if he has ears and a tail or not.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.620
Honestly, I'm done with it.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:58.880
Lost civilizations,

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.450
cryptids,

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:02.020
soulmates...

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.630
I'm a married woman.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:05.050
I don't believe in any of that one bit.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.380
<b>No More Occult Stuff</b>

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:09.760
Hii-kun.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.610
Let's eat udon. Udon!

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.520
Poco and I...

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:19.380
are friends forever!

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.460
Time to eat!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:27.650
Udon?

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:29.600
Er, yeah...

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.530
It's udon, but...

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.910
I cut it a little too big.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.270
But it should taste...

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:43.760
Mochi?

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.790
No, it's udon, Poco.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:50.030
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:53.800
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:57.420
Oh? Ya found his notes?

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:59.580
Yeah, but it's not as easy

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.690
as just following the recipe.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:03.310
Did ya mess it up?

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:05.630
Poco asked me if it was mochi.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:07.870
Sis!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.940
Ya cut 'em too big, didn't ya?

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:13.760
If I'd known...

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:18.090
If I'd known things would turn out like this, 
I would have paid more attention

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:20.660
when Dad was making udon.

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:22.210
Souta...

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:31.720
<b>Notes, Part 1</b>

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.960
I wish I'd talked to him more. 
About all sorts of things.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:30.330
I wish I'd spent more time with him.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:31.720
Yeah...

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:35.690
Listen, Souta.

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:40.200
I meant to bring this up on Shodoshima, 
but then there was all that fuss.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:43.110
Um, about Poco-chan...

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:44.130
Yeah?

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:48.640
You said you're gonna live with him. 
Were you serious about that?

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:50.010
Why do you ask?

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:53.900
Why do I... He's your friend's child, isn't he?

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.990
You can't stay together forever.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:59.630
Isn't it about time you thought about that?

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:03.080
You've gotta talk it over with Poco-chan, too.

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:06.770
Souta? Are ya listening?

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:09.420
Sorry. I'll call you later.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.500
Huh? Wait—

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.430
<i>I have to talk it over with Poco...</i>

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:15.620
Souta.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.430
I'm sowwy.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:21.140
I pwomised to make them go bye-bye...

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:27.050
Hey, Poco.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:29.570
We went to Tokyo, and then to Shodoshima.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:30.750
It was rough, huh?

00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:34.400
That must have really worn you out.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:36.830
You don't have to force anything.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:40.490
Listen, Poco...

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:43.390
If it's hard to stay human,

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:47.780
when we go to bed at night, 
you can turn back into a tanuki.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:50.030
Souta!

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:56.710
<i>What happened today might 
happen again in the future.</i>

00:17:57.480 --> 00:17:58.800
<i>If that happens, I...</i>

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:10.110
<i>It'll be okay.</i>

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:11.770
<i>It will.</i>

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:14.710
<i>I have to</i>

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:18.690
<i>do what I can to understand Poco better.</i>

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.820
<i>So we can always be together.</i>

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:37.100
I'll leave this here for you.

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:38.300
Thanks.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.430
Ah, yes. Sae...

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:42.550
What is it?

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:45.160
That man you introduced to me

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.460
at Ritsurin Garden, with the children...

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.970
Oh, you mean the man from Tawara Udon.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.260
The smaller child who was with him...

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.570
He said that wasn't his child.

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:57.830
He's not?

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:01.010
I assumed they were parent and child.

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:03.680
Do you suppose the child is still here?

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:08.140
I wonder. I don't know too much about them.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.700
Never mind, then.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:11.910
Okay.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:21.010
<b>The Tanuki Lore of Sanuki</b>

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:45.050
<b>Gaogao-chan and</b>

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:45.050
<b>The Blue Sky</b>

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:49.960
<i>The Tale of Gaogao-chan and Friends Forever!</i>

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:51.060
<b>Episode 9: "Gaogao-chan and Friends Forever"</b>

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.520
<i>From all the way across space,</i>

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.620
<i>in Galaxy M87,</i>

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:57.600
<i>Gaogao-chan's friend</i>

00:20:57.600 --> 00:20:59.960
<i>Gyaogyao-kun came to play.</i>

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:03.670
<i>We don't have much to offer, 
but make yourself at home.</i>

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:06.480
<i>Don't speak to me unless spoken to, Earthling.</i>

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:08.620
<i>Here you go.</i>

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:16.250
<i>Gross! It tastes like Earthlings, gyao!</i>

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:20.000
<i>Hey! That's no way to talk!</i>

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.840
<i>Don't touch me. I'll catch your stupidity, gyao.</i>

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.960
<i>Gaogao-chan, say something!</i>

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.690
<i>This guy is way too rude!</i>

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:30.270
<i>Gaogao, what's their problem?</i>

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:32.810
<i>They're too impudent for servants, gyao.</i>

00:21:33.110 --> 00:21:34.960
<i>Those Earthlings... No.</i>

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:36.130
<i>Mimi and Momo...</i>

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.300
<i>are my friends, gao.</i>

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:39.700
<i>Gaogao-chan!</i>

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:42.740
<i>What? You're friends with Earthlings?</i>

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:46.960
<i>Just as you are a dear friend to me,</i>

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.490
<i>Mimi and Momo are also my dear friends, gao.</i>

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:54.590
<i>B-But they don't have fangs or spikes.</i>

00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:57.430
<i>Earthlings are weird, gyao!</i>

00:21:57.800 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>If you hurt them,</i>

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.880
<i>I will not forgive you, gao. 
Yes, not even you.</i>

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.760
<i>Are you serious, gyao?</i>

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:08.000
<i>Very, gao.</i>

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:13.890
<i>I hate Earthlings, gyao. But...</i>

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:16.910
<i>No matter who you call a friend,</i>

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:20.370
<i>you will always be Gaogao to me, gyao.</i>

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:21.550
<i>See ya.</i>

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:24.790
<i>See you all again.</i>

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:29.200
<i>What did that mean?</i>

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:33.810
<i>That we are friends forever.</i>

00:22:32.230 --> 00:22:34.110
<i>S-Stop it, Gyao!</i>

